<title>BELGIUM: EU adopts clipped oats tariff quota.</title>
<headline>EU adopts clipped oats tariff quota.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-03-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>The European Union's cereals management committee has adopted changes simplifying the regulation allowing a tariff-free annual quota of 10,000 tonnes of clipped oats, a Commission official said on Friday.</p>
<p>The quota, agreed to compensate for enlargement of the European Union in 1995, was adopted in December to apply from January 1, 1996.</p>
<p>&quot;Since then the customs codes have changed and so the committee adopted changes to make the quota arrangements clearer,&quot; the official said.</p>
<p>Clipped oats are used mainly for feeding horses and although the quota is open to all countries the main beneficiary is Canada. -- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
</text>
